  "title": "Attentive Probing of Patch Tokens Complements Backbone Fusion for In-the-Wild Plant Disease Recognition",
  "version": "1.41",
  "captions": {
    "1": "Single-backbone classifiers. (a) DINOv2-L attentive probe compared with adding the DINOv3-L and CLIP-L probes, in the three settings. (b) Three classifiers on each backbone, official PlantWild. (c) DINOv2-L controls, official PlantWild.",
    "2": "Three-backbone comparisons. (a) Accuracy and difference from the three-probe fusion. (b) Estimates for the main swap.",
    "3": "Errors corrected by the attentive probe. (a) Within-host and host contributions to the accuracy gain, from the class-token probe and from the three-probe fusion. (b) Corrected images also corrected by the added backbones. (c) Contribution to the accuracy gain by the health state of the image.",
    "4": "Base-probe choice and the attentive gain. (a) PlantWild, 30 matched subsamples of the training images. (b) In-sample and out-of-fold training logits for the attentive branch, official PlantWild. (c) PlantSeg, base C selected by the base probe alone or by the attentive probe.",
    "5": "Datasets and frozen backbones."
  },
